> 
> `266-274`: **Coroutine not started + wrong null‑guard → animations won’t run and possible NRE.**
> 
> - Calling `PlayAnimations()` without `StartCoroutine` is a no‑op for an `IEnumerator`.
> - The else‑branch checks `_rewardBoxParent` but toggles `_rewardBox`, which can NRE if `_rewardBox` is null.
> 
> 
> Apply this diff:
> 
> ```diff
>      public void SetRewardBoxVisible(bool visible)
>      {
>          if (visible)
>          {
>              _hasCardPackRewards = false;
> -            PlayAnimations();
> -            _rewardBox.SetActive(visible);
> +            StartCoroutine(PlayAnimations());
> +            if (_rewardBox != null)
> +                _rewardBox.SetActive(true);
>              return;
>          }
> 
> -        if (_rewardBoxParent != null)
> -            _rewardBox.SetActive(false);
> +        if (_rewardBox != null)
> +            _rewardBox.SetActive(false);
>          if (_parent != null)
>              _parent.SetActive(false);
>      }
> ```
> 
> Optional: keep this API a pure visibility setter and trigger collection via a dedicated `CollectRewards()` method to avoid surprising side effects.
> 
> 
> Also applies to: 276-280
> 
> </blockquote></details>
