<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (14)</summary><blockquote>

<details>
<summary>Assets/Scripts/UI/Utils/VisibilityController.cs (8)</summary><blockquote>

`8-9`: **Prevent duplicate controllers on the same GameObject**

Guard against double-toggling by disallowing multiple components.


```diff
- public class VisibilityController : MonoBehaviour
+ [DisallowMultipleComponent]
+ public class VisibilityController : MonoBehaviour
```

---

`21-28`: **Apply state on enable; cache earlier**

Cache in Awake and re-apply whenever the component is enabled (covers re-enable cases and avoids 1st-frame flicker).



```diff
-    private void Start()
+    private void Awake()
     {
         // Cache all renderers and UI elements
         CacheChildComponents();
-        
-        // Apply initial visibility state
-        SetVisibility(isVisible);
     }
+    
+    private void OnEnable()
+    {
+        // Apply initial or current visibility whenever enabled
+        SetVisibility(isVisible);
+    }
```

Please confirm nothing upstream relies on Start ordering for visibility.

---

`10-16`: **Add switches: includeSelf and Canvas toggle gating**

Two toggles reduce surprises and unnecessary UI rebuilds:
- includeSelf: control whether the root’s own components are affected.
- toggleCanvasComponent: gate Canvas.enabled flips (CanvasGroup is often sufficient and cheaper).


```diff
     [Header("Visibility Settings")]
     [SerializeField] private bool isVisible = true;
     [SerializeField] private bool includeInactiveChildren = true;
+    [SerializeField] private bool includeSelf = true;
+    [Tooltip("If true, also toggles Canvas.enabled. Leave off to prefer CanvasGroup-only for cheaper UI show/hide.")]
+    [SerializeField] private bool toggleCanvasComponent = false;
```

---

`33-56`: **Filter out root components when desired and prep for baseline capture**

Exclude components on the same GameObject when includeSelf is false. Also clear any baseline caches if you add them (see next comment).


```diff
     private void CacheChildComponents()
     {
         childRenderers.Clear();
         childCanvases.Clear();
         childCanvasGroups.Clear();

         // Get all renderers in children (including inactive if specified)
         Renderer[] renderers = GetComponentsInChildren<Renderer>(includeInactiveChildren);
         childRenderers.AddRange(renderers);
+        if (!includeSelf)
+            childRenderers.RemoveAll(r => r != null && r.gameObject == gameObject);

         // Get all canvases in children
         Canvas[] canvases = GetComponentsInChildren<Canvas>(includeInactiveChildren);
         childCanvases.AddRange(canvases);
+        if (!includeSelf)
+            childCanvases.RemoveAll(c => c != null && c.gameObject == gameObject);

         // Get all canvas groups in children
         CanvasGroup[] canvasGroups = GetComponentsInChildren<CanvasGroup>(includeInactiveChildren);
         childCanvasGroups.AddRange(canvasGroups);
+        if (!includeSelf)
+            childCanvasGroups.RemoveAll(g => g != null && g.gameObject == gameObject);
```

---

`17-20`: **Don’t clobber authoring-time states; capture and restore baselines**

Right now “show” blindly enables everything and sets CG to alpha=1/interactable=true, which can override intentional per-child settings. Capture initial states during cache and restore them when visible; only force-off when hidden.


```diff
-    private List<Renderer> childRenderers = new List<Renderer>();
-    private List<Canvas> childCanvases = new List<Canvas>();
-    private List<CanvasGroup> childCanvasGroups = new List<CanvasGroup>();
+    private List<Renderer> childRenderers = new List<Renderer>();
+    private List<Canvas> childCanvases = new List<Canvas>();
+    private List<CanvasGroup> childCanvasGroups = new List<CanvasGroup>();
+
+    // Baseline states captured at cache-time
+    private readonly Dictionary<Renderer, bool> rendererInitialEnabled = new();
+    private readonly Dictionary<Canvas, bool> canvasInitialEnabled = new();
+    private readonly Dictionary<CanvasGroup, (float alpha, bool interactable, bool blocksRaycasts)> canvasGroupInitial = new();
```

And populate/restore:

```diff
 private void CacheChildComponents()
 {
+    rendererInitialEnabled.Clear();
+    canvasInitialEnabled.Clear();
+    canvasGroupInitial.Clear();
@@
     childRenderers.AddRange(renderers);
@@
+    foreach (var r in childRenderers)
+        if (r != null && !rendererInitialEnabled.ContainsKey(r))
+            rendererInitialEnabled[r] = r.enabled;
@@
     childCanvases.AddRange(canvases);
@@
+    foreach (var c in childCanvases)
+        if (c != null && !canvasInitialEnabled.ContainsKey(c))
+            canvasInitialEnabled[c] = c.enabled;
@@
     childCanvasGroups.AddRange(canvasGroups);
@@
+    foreach (var g in childCanvasGroups)
+        if (g != null && !canvasGroupInitial.ContainsKey(g))
+            canvasGroupInitial[g] = (g.alpha, g.interactable, g.blocksRaycasts);
```

```diff
 public void SetVisibility(bool visible)
 {
     isVisible = visible;
@@
-    foreach (Renderer renderer in childRenderers)
+    foreach (Renderer renderer in childRenderers)
     {
         if (renderer != null)
         {
-            renderer.enabled = visible;
+            if (visible)
+                renderer.enabled = rendererInitialEnabled.TryGetValue(renderer, out var e) ? e : true;
+            else
+                renderer.enabled = false;
         }
     }
@@
-    foreach (Canvas canvas in childCanvases)
+    foreach (Canvas canvas in childCanvases)
     {
         if (canvas != null)
         {
-            canvas.enabled = visible;
+            if (toggleCanvasComponent)
+            {
+                if (visible)
+                    canvas.enabled = canvasInitialEnabled.TryGetValue(canvas, out var e) ? e : true;
+                else
+                    canvas.enabled = false;
+            }
         }
     }
@@
-    foreach (CanvasGroup canvasGroup in childCanvasGroups)
+    foreach (CanvasGroup canvasGroup in childCanvasGroups)
     {
         if (canvasGroup != null)
         {
-            canvasGroup.alpha = visible ? 1f : 0f;
-            canvasGroup.interactable = visible;
-            canvasGroup.blocksRaycasts = visible;
+            if (visible)
+            {
+                if (canvasGroupInitial.TryGetValue(canvasGroup, out var s))
+                {
+                    canvasGroup.alpha = s.alpha;
+                    canvasGroup.interactable = s.interactable;
+                    canvasGroup.blocksRaycasts = s.blocksRaycasts;
+                }
+                else
+                {
+                    canvasGroup.alpha = 1f;
+                    canvasGroup.interactable = true;
+                    canvasGroup.blocksRaycasts = true;
+                }
+            }
+            else
+            {
+                canvasGroup.alpha = 0f;
+                canvasGroup.interactable = false;
+                canvasGroup.blocksRaycasts = false;
+            }
         }
     }
```

---

`75-83`: **Gate Canvas.enabled flips (can be expensive)**

Disabling a Canvas forces rebuilds and breaks batching. Prefer CanvasGroup-only for show/hide and gate Canvas toggles behind a flag (added above).

---

`124-132`: **Auto-refresh option on hierarchy changes**

If children are added/removed at runtime, offer an opt-in auto-refresh using OnTransformChildrenChanged.


```diff
     public void RefreshCache()
     {
         CacheChildComponents();
         SetVisibility(isVisible);
     }
+
+    [SerializeField] private bool autoRefreshOnHierarchyChanged = false;
+    private void OnTransformChildrenChanged()
+    {
+        if (autoRefreshOnHierarchyChanged)
+            RefreshCache();
+    }
```

---

`147-157`: **Clarify editor preview semantics**

OnValidate only runs this in Play Mode, so “editorPreview” is a bit misleading. Either rename it (e.g., applyDuringPlayInEditor) or support true edit-time preview via ExecuteAlways (be careful to avoid scene dirties).



If you want true edit-time preview, I can propose a safe ExecuteAlways pattern that doesn’t dirty scenes.

